### `GET /api/history?metric=<key>[&days=<n>]`
Returns `[[ts, value], ...]` (ts = ISO 8601 with ET offset, oldest first) for one metric since 12:00 AM ET today by default (a value known before midnight is re-stamped at 00:00; `days=<n>` for a rolling span; stored history is never trimmed), merged from `metrics-history.jsonl` and `metrics-history-rebuilt.jsonl` and cached by both files' mtime/size. Rebuilt or backfilled points carry a third element `1` (`[ts, value, 1]`). Keys: the 10 tile keys, `artist:<name>`, `job:<id>`. Unknown key or no data -> `[]`.

## 5. Running it
```
cd "<root>/docs/play-on-words/live-board"
nohup python3 server.py >> server.log 2>&1 &     # detach in its own session
```
Optional environment variables: `PENWORK_ROOT` (project root) and `PENWORK_BOARD_PORT` (default 47321). Generated files that sit next to `server.py`: `window-baseline.json`, `jobs-window-baseline.json`, `catalog-artists.json`, `confirmed-seq.json`, `metrics-history.jsonl` (append-only trend history) and `metrics-history-rebuilt.jsonl` (one-time 24h reconstruction). Never delete `confirmed-seq.json`, because it holds the permanent numbers.
